explanation:
The definition does not define a mathematical object. It is a composite of three isomorphisms used as a proof step:
1. local cohomology on f⁻¹V is identified with the homology of the sections of a global injective resolution;
2. a homology map induced by an isomorphism of section complexes;
3. an isomorphism with the homology of the pushed-forward resolution.

It is a stepping stone. Lemmas later in the file prove that it is natural in V and in the coefficient sheaf (`..._hom_open_naturality`, `..._hom_coefficient_naturality`). The file then assembles it, via `NatIso.ofComponents` (around line 980), into the identification of the presheaf of derived pushforwards with V ↦ H^q(f⁻¹V, G). So it is bookkeeping for a proof — the content of a lemma packaged as an isomorphism — not a standalone notion that could be compared against a textbook definition.
